# Atoms Inspector Extension

`extension/` is a Chrome extension (Manifest V3) that inspects running pages for Atoms components and tokens. It is a consumer of this repo, never part of the published package.

- **One direction only.** `extension/` may import from `src/tokens`, `src/release/version`, and read `src/components` / `src/index.ts` at build time. Atoms Studio (`extension/src/studio/`) also imports the library's public entry `src/index.ts`, `src/theme` and `data/components.json`, so it renders designs with the real components and builds prop controls from their documented types. Nothing under `src/` or `app/` imports from `extension/`.
- **Keep it out of the package.** The library ships `dist/` from the `tsup` entries only. Never add an extension entry to `tsup.config.ts` or a path to `package.json` `files`.
- **No hand-copied tokens.** Token names and values come from `src/tokens` at build time. A token sync needs `npm run build:extension`, not an edit here.
- **Library changes arrive by rebuild.** Because the build reads the library, a component change needs `npm run pack:extension` and a `manifest.json` version bump, not an edit here. The exceptions are the special cases written for one component — `STARTERS` in `studio/Insert.tsx`, the grid's `gridCells` / `withCells`, `CLONED` in `src/mcp/screen-code.ts`, the marks readers. They are listed in section 6 of `30-components.mdc`, which loads when library code is edited. Add a row there whenever you add a case like these here.
- **Component names come from `displayName`.** `extension/build.mjs` keeps each `displayName` literal that `src/index.ts` exports. A new component is picked up once it sets `displayName` and is exported.
- **Shadow DOM only.** Everything the inspector draws lives in its shadow root. It never writes styles or attributes onto the inspected page.
- **Marks are the contract.** A development build of Atoms writes `--atoms-<property>: "<token>"` and `--atoms-v` in its CSS (`src/components/_shared/devMarks.ts`) and `data-atoms-pattern` / `data-atoms-region` on pattern regions. Token paths on both sides come from `src/tokens/paths.ts` — never re-derive them here.
- **Drift is declared versus rendered.** A row is `exact` when the rendered value is the declared token's value for the current mode, `drift` otherwise, and the note names the cause (`style`, `sx`, outside CSS, mode, version). An unmarked winning rule is the component's own choice, not drift.
- **Own tsconfig.** The root `tsconfig.json` excludes `extension/`. Check it with `npm run typecheck:extension`.
- **Screenshots go through the bridge.** The inspector runs in the page's main world, which has no `chrome.*`. `src/bridge.ts` runs in the isolated world, relays capture requests to the background worker (`chrome.tabs.captureVisibleTab` under `activeTab`), and answers only while the inspector is open and right after a click. No new permissions.
- **The export is read, not guessed.** `inspector/handover.ts` builds the `atoms-screen` JSON from the fiber tree: Atoms components with the props the caller wrote, layout primitives, plain elements matched to tokens. What a component draws inside itself stays out, except content the caller passed in. Bump `HANDOVER_FORMAT_VERSION` on any change that breaks a reader.
- **Studio is a consumer app.** It renders the handover tree inside an iframe with its own Emotion cache and `ThemeProvider` (`documentNode` / `colorSchemeNode` point at the iframe), so the design sees the canvas width and mode, not Studio's. Nodes in that iframe belong to another window: never test them with `instanceof`, and read their computed style with `styleOf` (their own window). Studio measures with the inspector's own `measure`, `overlay` and `rows`, so a selection reads the same in both.
- **Edits stay inside the system.** Studio edits props from `data/components.json`, and styles only through token pickers. A component changed outside its props — size, padding, type, icon size, colour, border, on the component or on a part of it — is stored in `overrides` (`src/studio/overrides.ts`: the key is the property, optionally after the part's selector; the value a token path, or pixels for sizes) and always exported as a deviation.
- **Storage is IndexedDB in the extension origin** (`src/shared/db.ts`), shared by the background worker and Studio. The handover format lives in `src/shared/schema.ts`; Studio still reads version 1 files. The Atoms MCP's `build_from_json` (`src/mcp/screen-code.ts` at the repo root) reads the same schema, so a format change is a change to that tool too — keep what it reads (`VISUAL_KEY`, the readme's `BUILD_LINE`) in the schema module, not in inspector code.
